  "version": "1-ch12-pilot",
  "rule": "Sense-constant term policy (GITA_FULL_TRANSLATION_PLAN.md §4). A Sanskrit lemma is kept in IAST for a recorded sense only when all three tests pass: (1) the Gītā uses it as a category of its own system in that sense; (2) no English word or short phrase carries that sense without adding or dropping; (3) keeping it loses nothing because the card and glossary carry the meaning. Otherwise the (lemma, sense) is translated with ONE fixed rendering. Every word card whose stem or part matches a lemma below MUST carry `term: {lemma, sense}`; `check_gita_terms.js` enforces the rendering on every occurrence. Decisions are global across readers; rows marked `review: pilot` are open for the owner at the chapter-12 gate (O3). A new lemma or sense is added here deliberately, never ad hoc in a card.",
  "detectors_note": "`match` is a regex tested against each of: stem, iast, every parts[].form and every compound member, separately (so ^ means word start). A preserve row may list `iast_forms` (derived or inflected IAST prints that count as printing the term).",
